  "raw_text": "The naming of the drives as inference_1 and inference_2 was a declaration that changed the identity of the storage layer. The user rejected the word \"tension\" \u2014 an overloaded LLM term that had accumulated too much ambient noise to function as a clean identifier \u2014 and chose the project's own operative vocabulary instead. This is a harmony_restoration through lexical sovereignty: the backup medium is now named after the artifacts it protects, making the drive label a tribal signal readable to anyone inside the project's conceptual field. The renaming also introduced an underscore convention that the user explicitly motivated on perceptual grounds (1 and lowercase l look alike), a manner-cooperative act that encodes human legibility directly into the naming standard.",
